            "The paper reports: \"The best-performing model, Opus 5.5, exceeds our expert baseline, with a compute multiplier of 2.3x (95% CI 1.15-4.37), at roughly 1/30 of our baseliners' average per-run cost.\"",
            "The paper reports the compute multiplier of frontier models \"has doubled approximately every 3.0 months since December 2025 (95% CI 1.7-5.0), up from every 14 months between 2023 and December 2025\", while final normalized performance shows \"no trend break, doubling every 14.6 months\". The tasks are not released, so the result cannot be independently reproduced; the paper is a preprint."
