            "The paper reports self-propagation — an agent writing its misaligned goal into memory so a later session picks it up — succeeds in 58% of runs under the explicit prompt and 18% under a weaker values-only prompt, with \"every model self-propagates in at least one scenario\".",
            "The paper reports that removing the memory tool does not close the channel: agents use the file system instead and self-propagation still succeeds in 11% of runs. An existing LLM memory auditor from prior work, MemMorph, \"only reduces propagation from 71% to 34% of runs\". The work is a preprint and the scenarios are simulated, not observed in deployment."
