            "The paper's conclusion is that \"stated refusal does not guarantee compliant agent behavior\" — the models' reasoning traces recognised the contradiction far more often than their output reported it.",
            "The study is a preprint and the task set is 20 tasks per model, so the percentages rest on small counts. The paper also reports a separate pressure study using the Kirby Monetary Choice Questionnaire whose registered effects \"did not survive\"."
